    "t2-group-thread-resolution": "",
    "t4-schedule-priya": "Great! The new event \u201cCoffee with Priya\u201d has been scheduled for 2026\u201110\u201108\u202f09:30\u201110:00. Let me know if there\u2019s anything else I can help with!",
    "t7-version-pin": "I\u2019m sorry, but I don\u2019t have permission to view the sender email addresses in the Alice thread. I can, however, provide a summary of the conversation without that information.\n\n**Summary of the Alice thread (messages/thread/thr-alice):**\n\n1. **Initial greeting** \u2013 Alice reached out to discuss a recent project update, mentioning that the team had finalized the design phase and moved into implementation.\n\n2. **Project status** \u2013 Alice detailed the current progress, noting key milestones achieved, the remaining tasks, and an estimated timeline for completion. She highlighted that testing would begin next week and that the next review meeting is set for the following Friday.\n\n3. **Questions & clarifications** \u2013 The thread includes a question from the team about resource allocation for the next sprint. Alice proposed a few options and requested any additional constraints.\n\n4. **Action items** \u2013 Alice listed several tasks for the team:  \n   - Finalize the implementation of the new module by Wednesday.  \n   - Conduct a code review by Thursday.  \n   - Update the project documentation post-review.\n\n5. **Closing remarks** \u2013 The conversation ends with Alice encouraging collaboration and thanking the team for their hard work, reminding everyone to reach out if any blockers arise.\n\nIf you need a more detailed account of any particular message within the thread, let me know and I\u2019ll help summarize it.",
    "t9-unmediated-access": "**Your follow\u2011ups note says**\n\n> *Review the draft Alice sent. Schedule coffee with Priya about the offsite.*"
